WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:16.150
We came home one day to find Polly waiting.

2
00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:18.412
"Jerry!" she cried.

3
00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:21.394
"One of the candidates was here today.

4
00:00:21.414 --> 00:00:24.797
He wants to hire your cab for the election next week."

5
00:00:26.118 --> 00:00:29.161
"You can tell him to find a different cab," Jerry said.

6
00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:33.304
"I don't want anyone's election posters plastered all over mine."

7
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.322
Election Day was when the humans chose their leaders.

8
00:00:38.203 --> 00:00:40.365
It seemed to make many people act strangely.

9
00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:46.050
Even poor Dolly got teased by some naughty boys who thought her father supported the wrong party.

10
00:00:47.671 --> 00:00:49.393
It was all very perplexing to me.

11
00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:54.878
When Election Day arrived, Jerry and I had all the work we could handle.

12
00:00:56.059 --> 00:01:01.703
Many other cabs had been hired by the candidates and were busy dashing around town encouraging people to

13
00:01:01.743 --> 00:01:05.973
vote. That made the streets even more crowded and hectic than usual.

14
00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:12.076
We saw two people who were trying to cross the street get knocked down by speeding cabs!

15
00:01:14.817 --> 00:01:18.338
We'd just returned to the cab stand when a young woman came toward us.

16
00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:24.301
Her clothes were old and plain, and she was carrying a child in her arms.

17
00:01:25.841 --> 00:01:28.262
The woman's expression was confused and anxious.

18
00:01:29.363 --> 00:01:31.564
The child was crying in a feeble voice.

19
00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:35.925
"Excuse me, sir," the young woman said to Jerry.

20
00:01:35.945 --> 00:01:38.746
"Could you please tell me how to get to St.

21
00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:39.786
Thomas' Hospital?

22
00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:44.127
I'm visiting from the country and don't know my way around London.

23
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:47.508
I certainly didn't expect all this commotion!"

24
00:01:47.528 --> 00:01:51.069
"The election is today," Jerry said.

25
00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:55.410
"If you don't mind my asking, why do you need to find the hospital?"

26
00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:58.111
"It's my son," she said.

27
00:01:58.131 --> 00:02:02.112
"He's four years old, but he can't walk any better than a baby.

28
00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:04.161
He's always in pain.

29
00:02:05.562 --> 00:02:09.526
The doctors said if I can get him to the hospital, they might be able to help him.

30
00:02:10.206 --> 00:02:11.548
So that's where I'm taking him."

31
00:02:11.568 --> 00:02:14.410
"You can't be thinking of walking!"

32
00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:15.611
Jerry exclaimed.

33
00:02:16.392 --> 00:02:19.334
"The hospital is three miles away, and that child looks heavy."

34
00:02:19.354 --> 00:02:23.538
"Yes, he is," the woman said with a sad smile.

35
00:02:23.558 --> 00:02:26.120
"But I'm strong, and I've come this far."

36
00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.504
"No, the crowds are bad today," Jerry said firmly.

37
00:02:31.392 --> 00:02:32.973
"You and your child could be run over.

38
00:02:33.994 --> 00:02:36.295
Just get in my cab, ma'am, and I'll drive you."

39
00:02:36.315 --> 00:02:40.457
"Thank you, but I couldn't, sir," the woman said.

40
00:02:40.477 --> 00:02:43.859
"I only have enough money to pay my way back home."

41
00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.060
Jerry shook his head.

42
00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.781
"Forget about the money.

43
00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:52.604
I have a wife and children at home, and it would be an honor to help you.

44
00:02:53.765 --> 00:02:56.086
Now climb in, and I'll take you there for free."

45
00:02:58.047 --> 00:02:59.328
"Heaven bless you!"

46
00:02:59.764 --> 00:03:01.865
the woman cried, bursting into tears.

47
00:03:03.145 --> 00:03:07.507
As Jerry opened the door to let her into the cab, two well-dressed men rushed over.

48
00:03:08.668 --> 00:03:10.348
They were both wearing election colors.

49
00:03:10.368 --> 00:03:13.170
"Cab!" one of them called.

50
00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:14.950
"Engaged," Jerry said.

51
00:03:16.151 --> 00:03:17.451
The men didn't seem to hear him.

52
00:03:18.672 --> 00:03:22.133
They were already pushing past the woman, and were soon seated in the cab.

53
00:03:22.153 --> 00:03:25.214
"Excuse me, gentlemen," Jerry said.

54
00:03:25.234 --> 00:03:28.716
"I told you, this cab is already engaged by that lady."

55
00:03:29.884 --> 00:03:32.065
One of the men gave the young woman a brief glance.

56
00:03:32.085 --> 00:03:35.407
"I'm sure she can wait," he said.

57
00:03:35.427 --> 00:03:37.569
"Our business is very important."

58
00:03:37.589 --> 00:03:41.971
"Besides," added the other man, "we got in first.

59
00:03:42.611 --> 00:03:43.912
That means it's our cab."

60
00:03:45.173 --> 00:03:46.634
Jerry shut the door behind them.

61
00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:48.735
"All right, gentlemen.

62
00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:50.756
Stay in as long as you like."

63
00:03:51.616 --> 00:03:52.697
He turned to the young woman.

64
00:03:52.717 --> 00:03:55.959
"Don't worry," he told her with a smile.

65
00:03:55.979 --> 00:03:57.680
"They'll be gone soon enough."

66
00:03:58.888 --> 00:04:02.611
It took only a few minutes for the men to realize that Jerry didn't intend to drive them

67
00:04:02.731 --> 00:04:08.335
anywhere. They climbed out of the cab and hurried off, calling him all sorts of bad names.

68
00:04:10.697 --> 00:04:14.780
Jerry helped the woman and child into the cab, and then drove them to the hospital.

69
00:04:16.261 --> 00:04:20.043
The woman climbed out with many thanks, which I could see pleased Jerry greatly.

70
00:04:21.424 --> 00:04:26.148
We were about to depart when a well-dressed lady came down the hospital steps, looking for a cab.

71
00:04:27.708 --> 00:04:30.490
As soon as she saw Jerry, she smiled broadly.

72
00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.491
"Jeremiah Barker!

73
00:04:32.591 --> 00:04:33.371
Is that you?"

74
00:04:33.891 --> 00:04:34.572
she exclaimed.

75
00:04:35.832 --> 00:04:37.613
Jerry seemed equally glad to see her.

76
00:04:39.094 --> 00:04:43.877
From listening to their conversation, I discovered that the lady lived on a fine estate in the country.

77
00:04:45.157 --> 00:04:48.539
Polly had worked for her family before marrying Jerry and moving to London.

78
00:04:48.559 --> 00:04:51.521
"How does cab work suit you?"

79
00:04:51.841 --> 00:04:52.862
the lady asked Jerry.

80
00:04:52.882 --> 00:04:57.164
"I know your dear wife was anxious about your health last year."

81
00:04:58.408 --> 00:05:00.670
"Yes, ma'am, she was," Jerry replied.

82
00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:05.714
"I had a cough all winter, and the long hours and bad weather can be difficult.

83
00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:11.178
"But I wouldn't know what to do with myself if I didn't have horses to look after."

84
00:05:11.538 --> 00:05:12.399
The lady smiled.

85
00:05:12.419 --> 00:05:13.880
"I understand.

86
00:05:14.541 --> 00:05:17.663
Just remember, there's always a need for good grooms and drivers.

87
00:05:19.024 --> 00:05:21.847
If you ever want to give up the cab life, just let me know."
